INT. ABANDONED ARCADE, BACK ROOM - NIGHT

Dead pinball machines draped in sheets. A card table. Four chairs, one empty.

MAGDA KOWALCZYK, 50s, plans on a napkin. TWYLA BANKS, 30s, drums the table with a lighter. And JOSÉ "PINCH" ARRIAGA, 40s, folds the map in precise squares.

MAGDA
Three minutes in, four out.

TWYLA
Three in, three out.

MAGDA
She wants a margin.

TWYLA
She wants a lot of things.

PINCH
Who's the she?

TWYLA
The she who gets us paid.

The back door scrapes. A fourth figure ducks in, pulling a hood down from a bruised face. DEVANTE ROOK, 20s, the driver. He drops into the empty chair and doesn't speak.

MAGDA
You're late.

DEVANTE
The truck was followed.

PINCH
By who?

DEVANTE
A woman. Maybe two.

MAGDA
Where did you lose her?

DEVANTE
I didn't.

Silence. The pinball machines hum faintly under their sheets. Twyla's lighter stops clicking.

TWYLA
Then she's outside.

DEVANTE
She's outside.

MAGDA
Then we're finished.

PINCH
(folding the map)
No. We are retired.
